Now I have the complete picture. Let me summarize my findings:

## Root Cause

The bug is in `MessageBubble.tsx` lines 158-168, specifically the `streamingRemainder` calculation:

```typescript
let streamingRemainder: string | undefined;
if (hasSegments && message.isStreaming && message.content) {
    const segmentedText = message.segments!
        .filter((s) => s.type !== 'tool')
        .map((s) => s.text || '')
        .join('');
    const remaining = message.content.slice(segmentedText.length);
    if (remaining.trim()) {
        streamingRemainder = remaining;
    }
}
```

The filter excludes only `tool` segments, but `subagent_start` and `subagent_end` segments also contain text fields that aren't part of `message.content` since it only accumulates text from `onTextChunk` callbacks. When subagent segments are present, the calculated `segmentedText` incorrectly includes their text alongside the actual message content, causing the remainder calculation to be off.

This mismatch means `message.content.slice(segmentedText.length)` returns empty, so the streaming answer text never displays until `onDone` fires and creates the final segment all at once.

The fix is to change the filter to only include `thinking` and `answer` segments, ensuring we're only measuring text that actually exists in `message.content`.

